Changed: IBTK::PETScLevelSolver has the new protected virtual functions getLayoutKeySpecialized() and initializeCoefficientsSpecialized(). These functions split the data that depend only on the layout of the level from the data that depend on the coefficients. When initializeSolverState() initializes a solver that is already initialized, with an unchanged level, vectors, and options, and getLayoutKeySpecialized() returns true, IBTK::PETScLevelSolver calls initializeCoefficientsSpecialized() instead of initializeSolverStateSpecialized(). In that case, IBTK::PETScLevelSolver does not call generateASMSubdomains() or generateFieldSplitSubdomains(). IBTK::CCPoissonPETScLevelSolver, IBTK::SCPoissonPETScLevelSolver, IBTK::VCSCViscousPETScLevelSolver, and IBAMR::StaggeredStokesPETScLevelSolver override both functions. A subclass of one of these classes that overrides initializeSolverStateSpecialized(), generateASMSubdomains(), or generateFieldSplitSubdomains() must either override getLayoutKeySpecialized() to return false or override initializeCoefficientsSpecialized() and update the data of the other functions. Returning false makes every initialization a full one. Direct subclasses of IBTK::PETScLevelSolver see no change. The new virtual functions change the vtables of these classes.
<br>
(Boyce Griffith, 2026/11/25)
